      "annotations": [
        "The agent presents the person token via Signature-Key — the authorization endpoint requires one. Without it the resource answers 401 with requirement=person-token.",
        "A resource MUST have verified a person token before it issues a resource token, so the identity in the resource token is PS-asserted, not agent-asserted.",
        "KEY DIFFERENCE from four-party: aud = the PS URL, taken from the ps claim of the person token. The resource has no AS of its own.",
        "The resource token carries ps, sub and presented_jti copied from the person token, plus agent_jkt binding it to the agent's key. It carries no agent identifier.",
        "The same resource token can also arrive on a 401 with AAuth-Requirement: requirement=auth-token, when the agent calls an endpoint directly instead of the authorization endpoint."
