      "annotations": [
        "The agent sends the resource token to its PS's auth_token_endpoint (renamed from token_endpoint in -11). It signs with its own agent token, not the person token.",
        "The PS sees aud = its own URL — no federation needed. It is the authority.",
        "The PS looks up the person token named by presented_jti among those it issued and verifies ps, sub, mission_s256 and tenant match it exactly. Any mismatch is rejected.",
        "The PS verifies agent_jkt in the resource token is the JWK thumbprint of the key that signed this request.",
        "The PS issues the auth token: iss=PS, dwk=aauth-person.json, aud=resource, ps=PS, sub=the same directed identifier, cnf.jwk=the agent's public key.",
        "No AS is contacted. The PS is the sole token issuer in this mode."
